A. Commit message:
```
Allow tls-crypt-v2 setup only on the initial packet of a session

This fixes an internal server error condition that can be triggered by a
malicious authenticated client, unlucky packet corruption, or an attacker
injecting a specially crafted packet at the right time.

The error condition results in an ASSERT statement being triggered.

CVE: 2025-2704
```

B. Change summary:
```
- Added S_PRE_START_SKIP state to allow deferred processing of initial packets
- Modified read_control_auth to accept an additional 'initial_packet' parameter
- Updated tls_crypt_v2_extract_client_key to ignore wrapped keys if not an initial packet
- Adjusted state transitions in tls_pre_decrypt to account for S_PRE_START_SKIP
- Ensured proper handling of initial packets in tls_pre_decrypt_lite
```

C. Compatibility Risk:
Medium

